Goal
• We build a static site for Kras-Trans using: Jinja2 templates (templates/), CSS (assets/css/), JS (assets/js/), Python build (tools/), and pages.yml (GitHub Actions). No Shopify/Drupal/Liquid.
• All content comes from data/cms/menu.xlsx only. If data are missing, the section is not rendered (no placeholders).
• i18n languages: pl, en, de, fr, it, ru, ua with routes /{lang}/… (home at /{lang}/).

Working mode
• One task = one small change = one file. Show DIFF only.
• Large changes → ZIP preserving repo structure.
• Keep build/tests green.

Do not
• Do not edit dist/.
• Do not commit binary XLSX/ZIP via PR (menu.xlsx is uploaded via GitHub UI).
• Respect CODEOWNERS for data/cms/menu.xlsx.
• Do not bring external frameworks/tools unless explicitly requested.

CMS contract (short)
• Sheets: Pages, Nav, Blocks, Routes, Strings, props (headers match the contract).
• Pages: type=home|page, slugKey, slug, publish, order, h1, title, seo_title, meta_desc, lead, body_md.
• Nav: lang, label, href, parent, order(int), col(int), enabled; meta fields: nav.logo.src, nav.logo.alt, nav.cta.label, nav.cta.slugKey, nav.social.\*.
• Blocks: block, lang, page (slugKey), type (hero|list|bullets|cta|text…), title, lead, body_md, cta_label, cta_href, order, enabled.
• Routes: slugKey + language columns without prefixes ("home", "services", …).
• Strings/props: key -> per-language values (CTA text, metas, etc.).

Navigation / mega-menu
• Top-level <a> always navigates; <button.mega-toggle> opens the panel (aria-expanded/aria-controls + [hidden]/aria-hidden).
• Desktop hover (matchMedia '(hover:hover) and (pointer:fine)') opens mega; mobile uses click.
• Only one mega open; Esc/click-outside closes.
• Panel full-width (left:0; right:0; no horizontal scroll).
• Sorting: top-level by order (int; missing/invalid → 9999).
• Children grouped by col (int; missing=1) and sorted by order within each column.
• Language switcher with flag + code; clicking replaces the first URL segment with target language.

SEO / A11y
• base.html: <title> = seo_title || h1 || title; <meta name="description"> = meta_desc; canonical/hreflang/OG/JSON-LD as standard.
• Semantic HTML only; focus-visible; WCAG AA contrast; correct aria on toggles/panels.
• One h1 per page (preferably in hero); duplicate h1 from body can be visually hidden in CSS.

Performance
• Defer JS; avoid heavy runtimes.
• LCP < 2.5s (preload LCP image; lazy-load others); images later can be WebP/AVIF.
• No horizontal scroll; minimize CLS.

PR / CI rules
• Show DIFF only; one file per task.
• Acceptance criteria in description (what/where/how to verify).
• Tests: pytest must pass; local build: `python tools/build.py`.
• Do not change pages.yml unless explicitly instructed.

Globs to work on
• templates/**/_.html, assets/css/_.css, assets/js/_.js, tools/_.py, .github/workflows/pages.yml, data/**/\*.json (never dist/).

CSR fallback / API
• If a section needs runtime data, add `data-api` attributes and use a global `CMS_ENDPOINT` with a proper fallback to prebuilt data.

If a requested patch does not fit these principles — skip silently.
